>> title: BBQ Tofu Bowl
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: tofu, quinoa, brussels sprouts, barbecue, vegetarian, sheet pan, bowl
>> counters: The Bowl Shop
>> aka: bbq tofu bowl, barbecue tofu bowl, baked tofu bowl, glazed tofu bowl, quinoa bowl, vegetarian bowl, grain bowl, power bowl
>> pairs-with: barbecue-sauce, ranch-dressing
>> servings: 4
>> time: 1 hr 15 min
>> step.1: Press the tofu or the glaze slides straight off it. Twenty minutes under a weight is a coat that sticks.
>> step.2: press 20 min, then slab it
>> step.3: roast 450°F (230°C) 25 min, glaze, 5 min more
>> step.4: toast 3 min, simmer 15 min, rest 10 min
>> step.5: roast 450°F (230°C) 22 min, cut side down
>> step.6: build it, tofu and sprouts over the quinoa

Press the tofu or the glaze slides straight off it. Twenty minutes under a weight is the difference between a coat that sticks and a puddle in the bottom of the pan.

Press @firm tofu{14%oz}(400 g; halved through the middle) between towels under a weight ~press{20%min}, then cut it into 3/4-inch slabs.

Roast @&(~1)tofu{} tossed with @cornstarch{2%Tbs}, @vegetable oil{2%Tbs}(30 mL) and @kosher salt{1/2%tsp} on a #sheet pan{} at 450°F (230°C) ~roast{25%min}, turning once, until the edges are firm and gold, then brush it with @barbecue sauce{1/3%cup}(80 mL) and give it ~roast{5%min} more.

Toast @quinoa{1%cup}(170 g; rinsed and drained well) dry in a #saucepan{} ~toast{3%min}, until it smells nutty, then add @water{1 3/4%cups}(415 mL) and @kosher salt{1/2%tsp}, ~simmer{15%min} covered, and ~rest{10%min} off the heat.

Roast @Brussels sprouts{1%lb}(450 g; halved) tossed with @olive oil{2%Tbs}(30 mL) and @kosher salt{1/2%tsp} cut side down at 450°F (230°C) ~roast{22%min}, not turned, until the flat faces are nearly black.

Fork @&(~2)quinoa{} into four bowls, lay @&(~3)glazed tofu{} and @&(~1)roasted sprouts{} over it, and finish with @red onion{1/2}(sliced paper thin), @cider vinegar{1%Tbs}(15 mL), @flat-leaf parsley{1/4%cup}(chopped) and @ranch dressing{1/3%cup}(80 mL).
